`parse_m3u8_attributes` runs one loop iteration per regex match from `re.findall(...)`. Counting the attribute pairs in the 18 tests gives 30 total iterations. The invariant checks `',' not in val` at the end of the loop body, after optional quote stripping. Unquoted matches cannot contain commas because the regex branch for them is `[^",]+`, but quoted matches may contain commas inside the quotes, and stripping removes only the outer quotes. Across the test inputs, this happens in exactly three `CODECS` values: in tests `c`, `m`, and `q`. So there are 3 violating iterations out of 30, and the invariant does not always hold.

## Answer
{"total_iterations_observed":30,"violating_iteration_count":3,"is_invariant_always_held":false}
